B.P7=new A.eB("bodyplan_vehicle","Vehicle","","Gain +2 speed. You cannot climb. Forced movement targeting you is halved but damage from being forced into terrain is tripled.\nProne: When you are knocked prone, you cannot move nor dash, nor can you end the prone effect. Adjacent allies may spend a [Reaction] or [Action] to remove your prone.\nRiding: Adjacent allies may ride you, as long as at least 1 of their spaces can fit in your space, and that space doesn't contain another ally. For every space worth of ally unable to fit, reduce your speed by 1. While riding, players are prone, they may still be targeted for attacks, and they resist all damage and you take an equal amount of damage as they do if you were not also targeted by the attack. To begin riding and to stop riding players must pay the cost to stand from prone. Hexapod allies aren't damaged for becoming prone because of riding, and stop riding by spending 1 movement point.\nCollision: [Reaction] During your turn, you may move through an enemy who is a smaller size than you. Make a Status Check vs Str. On Success, deal {Vitality d12} Bludgeoning damage to you and the target and the target is knocked prone. On Problems, you take {Vitality d6} damage or are knocked prone.","",B.d0,B.ai3)
B.P0=new A.eZ("parts_universal","Universal"," Any of your allies may be your host, you can use a [Action] to move from your current host to a target ally. When an ally moves within {Half Level} spaces of you, you may spend your [Reaction] to move from your current host to that ally.","",B.d0)
B.OX=new A.eZ("parts_specific","Specific","You can only have a specific character be your host. At the end of your turn and your host turn, you and your host may give each other Shield and Health. During your turn, you may force your host to move up to {Half your speed}, this movement does provoke attacks. Whenever you or your host heals or gains shields you may give some or all of it to the other.","",B.d0)
B.af9=s([B.P0,B.OX],t.CT)
B.P9=new A.eB("bodyplan_parts","Parts","Your body is a part of another character\u2019s body. You are connected to your host and cannot be separated from each other. Effects that move, dash, teleport, slow, or restrain your host also apply to you and vise versa.You may not use movement points. When you take the [run] action, you may force your host to move up to your speed and this movement can provoke attacks. When you take the [Retreat] action, you may force your host to move half your speed without provoking attacks. When your host doesn\u2019t provoke attacks of opportunity, you also avoid attacks of opportunity. For each size you are more than your host, reduce their speed by 1. If you are smaller or larger than your host, you may reposition yourself relative to your host during your turn so that you are within at least 1 of their spaces. When you die, you must run a generic body with no combat features from spawn to a space adjacent to your host to respond in your body. When your host dies, you are stuck attached to their body until your host moves to space adjacent to you and uses an object interaction to pick you up. When you pick this, choose between being Universal, or Specific.","","",B.d0,B.af9)
