B.awe=new A.d5("source_vice","Sacrifice","The character gains their power through self destruction, like drinking or stamp collecting. When you activate a power, you lose {Vitality + Level} health, and activate the ability with a source of {Power + 1}. You cannot reduce sacrifice damage by any means.\nEach time you sacrifice, gain 1 suffering to a max of {points}. Suffering is lost at the end of the situation.\nWhen you pick this the first time, pick a below option that triggers before or after you sacrifice.","Whenever you or an ally you can see gets problems on a skill, pay {Vitality + Level} health to allow them to reroll. For the rest of the scene, you have either -1 to Conceal or Convince. Choose when you first take this.","Reduce your sacrifice health cost by {Half Vitality}.","At the start of your turn, make a Wis defense, or you must trigger a sacrifice ability on your turn. If you end your turn without having done so, pay {Vitality + Level} health. If this kills you, all allies must pass a Wis defense or have -1 to all checks until the end of the scene from guilt.","{Power + 1}",B.jr,"epic_source_vice",!1,"Suffering","{points}",B.af5,B.ajH,"{1}")
B.awW=new A.bP("Sprint","During your turn, you may pay stamina to move extra spaces. You move up to 2 spaces further for each stamina spent. This doesn't alter your speed. Whenever you are under an effect that reduces your speed, you move 1 space per stamina instead.",B.a0,!1)
B.awN=new A.bP("Dodge Roll","Before rolling a defense, you may spend {Vitality} stamina to gain advantage on the defense.",B.a0,!1)
B.awM=new A.bP("Follow through","On success with an attack that deals damage, you may spend up to {Half Power} stamina to deal 1d6 extra damage per stamina spent.",B.a0,!1)
B.ax2=new A.bP("Leap","[Reaction] During your turn or at the end of an ally\u2019s turn, [Reaction] and Pay up to {Vitality} stamina, and dash to a free space within 2 * paid stamina.",B.a0,!1)
B.awl=new A.bP("Stretch","Once per ability, you may pay 1 stamina to increase your range by 1.",B.a0,!1)
B.akh=s([B.awW,B.awN,B.awM,B.ax2,B.awl],t.AJ)
B.aw4=new A.d5("source_stamina","Stamina","The character gains their power through their physical endurance and strength. The character has {Power * points} Max Stamina, and regains all stamina at the end of the encounter. When they use a feature of this source, they may spend up to {Power} stamina, using the spent stamina as the source value. Breath: At the end of the round, if they haven't spent stamina this round, they gain {Power + Vitality} Stamina. For every 4 pts worth of combat features of the stamina source, gain 1 of the below abilities. You always know at least 1.","You may pay {half power} stamina to reroll a defense with a +1 to the result. You start the next encounter without this stamina.","During the next situation, whenever you Breath, regain {points / 3} extra stamina.","During the next situation, whenever you breathe, regain half the stamina.","{Power}",B.jr,"epic_source_stamina",!1,"Stamina","{Power * points}",B.akh,B.a0,"{points / 4}")
B.aw7=new A.d5("source_mutation","Mutation","You gain your powers from your body's ability to reorganize itself.\nYou have a Genepool of {points} combat features you select when you gain pts. You have {points} Evolution points at the start of every encounter. On your turn, You may spend evolution points to gain access to a feature in your genepool as a mutation. You may use the mutation for the remainder of the encounter with a source of {Half Power}. Mutations cost as many evolution points as they would feature points, and you may pay for upgrades up to the normal limit. You have a morph pool of {points / 3} Universal upgrades, and you may only use universal upgrades from your morph pool when you upgrade a mutation. When you trigger a mutation on later turns, you may pay for upgrades if possible. You may not exceed the normal feature upgrade limits. You must have a mutation to be able to use an ability in your genepool. You may pay twice the evolution cost of a mutation to give the mutation a source value of {Power} instead of {Half Power}.","{points / 3} times per Story, you may change your skill proficiencies or armor & fortitude values before making a check. This remains for the rest of the scene.","During the next situation: After activating a mutation ability, lose the mutation and regain those evolution points.","During the next situation, you reduce your max evolution points by 1.","{Half Power}",B.uG,"epic_source_mutation",!1,null,null,B.a0,B.a0,null)
B.LS=new A.p7(4,"time")
B.aw5=new A.d5("source_time","Time","The character gains their power through altering time or predicting the future. After each encounter, you may select your chronomancy from 1 to {half points}. Your time source is {power - chronomancy}. At the start of a story, Roll and record {Chronomancy +1} attacks and {Chronomancy +1} skills you are proficient in. When you use this source you use one of your applicable chronomancy results, then roll a replacement result.\nYour chronomancy results don't benefit from +1 or -1 to success. Whenever you have advantage or disadvantage, select 1 result then roll the extra check. If you gain a reroll, reroll as normal. When you change your chronomancy at the end of a situation, you pick which results are lost, and you only make new rolls for gained chronomancy. You may use an Implement gaining any implement effects. If you do, you require that type of implement to use the feature.","When you make a skill check you have a recorded result for, you may use one of your applicable chronomancy results instead of rolling, then roll a replacement result.","Reroll half of your chronomancy results.","Set half of your chronomancy results to 1.","{power - chronomancy}",B.LS,"epic_source_time",!0,"Chronomancy",null,B.a0,B.a0,null)
B.awn=new A.bP("Penetration","Pay 1 Psi Point and your ability ignores resistance.",B.a0,!1)
B.ax6=new A.bP("Drain","On Success, Pay up to {Half power} Additional Psi Points, to deal 1d6 extra damage and gain an equal amount of shield per Psi Point.",B.a0,!1)
B.awq=new A.bP("Focus","Pay 1 Psi Point, and attacks ignore advantage, disadvantage, -1 and +1 to results for the attack and defenses caused by the attack.",B.a0,!1)
B.awF=new A.bP("Distant","Pay 1 Psi Point and double the range of the ability or if the ability targets an area, increase the area size and range by 1.",B.a0,!1)
B.awQ=new A.bP("Phasing","Pay 1 Psi Point, and your movement doesn't provoke attacks of opportunity and you ignore difficult terrain.",B.a0,!1)
